{
  "title": "Refining Coarse-Grained Molecular Topologies with Bayesian Optimization",
  "authors": [
    "Pranoy Ray",
    "Adam P. Generale",
    "Nikhith Vankireddy",
    "Yuichiro Asoma",
    "Masataka Nakauchi",
    "Haein Lee",
    "Katsuhisa Yoshida",
    "Yoshishige Okuno",
    "Surya R. Kalidindi"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2401.12345",
  "abstract": "This work introduces a Bayesian Optimization-based approach to refine coarse-grained molecular dynamics (CGMD) simulations, specifically the bonded interaction parameters within a given coarse-grained mapping, for specialized applications. The resulting optimized CG potential accommodates any degree of polymerization, offering accuracy comparable to all-atom simulations while retaining the computational speed of CGMD.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Molecular Dynamics (MD) simulations are vital for predicting the physical and chemical properties of molecular systems. However, All-Atom (AA) MD simulations are computationally expensive, leading to the development of Coarse-Grained MD (CGMD) simulations, which simplify molecular structures into representative beads to reduce expense but sacrifice precision. This work aims to refine CGMD simulations using Bayesian Optimization (BO) to improve their accuracy and efficiency.",
